                <pb facs="0832" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">717.2114/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-15T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>180. Your 342, September 14, 9 a.m. Has text of treaty been published in Managua?
                    If so the issuance of a statement by the Department would be greatly
                    facilitated. It will be difficult for the Department to make a statement on this
                    subject to the press without giving the general terms of the treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
